# fixedbugs, defect 439, lane b14-resolve, 2026-10-07: `end_lease` takes one
# argument, the cell it frees (`check/lend_types.hero`), and the name stage
# held every `@` handed to it to the rule of the left of `@`, the second
# included, so `n` bound with `=` was told `not_mutable` where the call's own
# mistake is its second argument. The mark stays on the first argument alone
# now (`resolve/built_marks.hero`, `END_LEASE_WRITES`), and the checker tells
# the call. If `end_lease` ever takes a second `@`, this case moves.
#
# The checker's two messages are its own, the same on the base with `n` a
# cell: the second, *this argument is not such a cell*, is said of a call
# whose `@c` is a lease's cell, reported beside defect 439 by its lane.

function main()
    c: cstr @= "abc".lease()
    n = 1
    end_lease(@c, @n)  #~ builtin_shape
    print(n)

# Corrected 2026-10-07 at batch 14's gate, below the program so no line moves:
# defect 458 (lane b14-check, `9e9af1ad`) removed the second message this case
# pinned, *this argument is not such a cell*, false of `@c`; a call with an
# argument too many is told its count alone. The interaction of two repairs of
# one batch, 439's case written before 458's repair, redone here as the later
# one (`.claude/rules/verification.md` § The batch, *Red*).
